  >>> tf.reshape(t, [-1, 2])
  <tf.Tensor: shape=(3, 2), dtype=int32, numpy=
    array([[1, 2],
           [3, 4],
           [5, 6]], dtype=int32)>

  `tf.reshape(t, [])` reshapes a tensor `t` with one element to a scalar.

  >>> tf.reshape([7], []).numpy().item()
  7

  More examples:

